{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=February 2014}}
Group E was one of eight groups at the [[1998 FIFA World Cup]] into which the 32 teams were divided.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/98full.html |title=World Cup 1998 |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> Mexico and the Netherlands qualified after they both beat South Korea and drew with Belgium before drawing with each other. The Netherlands' five goals against South Korea put them top on goal difference. Belgium could have qualified with a big win in their final game against South Korea, who were already out, but they only managed a draw and were eliminated.

